  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Save the Children Sweden - REJ Programme</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Save the Children Sweden - REJ Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">The Save the Children programme on &quot;Giving Rights to the Silent Majority Children has
been funded by the Embassy of Sweden since 2008 Annual reports and various field visits done by the Embassy staff have shown that there is a clear direction towards achieveing the objectives
set at both outcome and impact level. There are significant and very relevant qualitative results at both the national, district and district level. It is clear that the Government and other key stakeholders are recognising the benefits of the multisectoral approach in addressing child rights governance matters.
Furthermore, the project has demonstrated that the Government is consistently and gradually
taking over coordination and ownership of the child rights governance mechanisms. The programme is
suggested to be extended for the period January - June 2015 in order to provide an opportunity for a development of a comprehensive child rights governanace and child protection programme and systematic phaseout of the current support. During this period the key focus will be on strengthening the enabling environment for sustainability of the programme interventions through more focused advocacy activities, strengthening accountability and child safeguarding and children&apos;s councils, documentation of results and more indepth work with media partners to
promote increased knowledge about child rights and legal provisions for general public, victims and potential victims.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the project is to empower and build the capacity of  most vulnerable children in 7 districts in Tanzania so that they can  claim their rights to protection, health care &amp; obtain appropriate    support from quality social, political, economic &amp; legal systems from community to national level.the primary focus is to support children  and key duty bearers to identify and adress child rights violation.</narrative>
  </description>
